<title>FRANCE: Sanofi starts Clopidogrel registration.</title>
<headline>Sanofi starts Clopidogrel registration.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French pharmaceuticals group Sanofi said on Monday that it had started the registration procedure in the U.S. and Europe for clopidogrel as an anti-thrombosis drug.</p>
<p>Clopidogrel, developed jointly with Bristol-Myers Squibb Co, is a major product in Sanofi's line-up of future drugs.</p>
<p>The company had said it would make a registration in the first quarter of 1997 back in November when the so-called CAPRIE clinical trial showed the drug was &quot;significantly more effective than aspirin at reducing the likelihood of ischemic stroke, heart attack or vascular death in at-risk patients&quot;.</p>
<p>Clopidogrel is the second product stemming from a 1993 co-operation pact with Bristol-Myers after Irbesartan, for which registration was started in october 1996.</p>
<p>Sanofi is majority-owned by oil group Elf-Aquitaine.</p>
